WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.780
Add a second machine.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.660
Both machines need Tailscale, signed in to the same account,

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.020
with MagicDNS and HTTPS certificates turned on.

4
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:16.453
On the new machine, here a Mac mini, open Settings, then Connections.

5
00:00:16.453 --> 00:00:21.826
Choose Invite this machine, give it a name, and choose Make the line.

6
00:00:21.826 --> 00:00:26.443
SpecWithCode publishes itself on the Mac mini's private Tailscale name,

7
00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:28.408
never on the public internet.

8
00:00:28.408 --> 00:00:32.270
The line works like a password, so it stays blurred here.

9
00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:36.077
On your main machine, open the same Connections page.

10
00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:40.651
Paste the line under Add a machine, and choose Add machine.

11
00:00:40.651 --> 00:00:44.449
The main machine checks that the address answers as that Mac,

12
00:00:44.449 --> 00:00:48.750
then lists it as reachable. Its address is blurred too.

13
00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.740
Pick the most a worker there may do.

14
00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:57.930
Version 1.0.47 also asks for a one-time pairing code from the Mac mini,

15
00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:01.087
made there beforehand with specwithcode pair.

16
00:01:01.087 --> 00:01:07.050
Then choose Allow workers. The card now reads Allowed: Full access.

17
00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:12.230
Next: add a Linux server you rent, with the Linux worker guide.
